The 3DS cameras from the frontend's, through libretro's camera interface

The libretro core registered no camera, so every 3DS camera was the blank one:
a game that photographs, or reads a QR code, saw black. This adds a camera
backed by RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_CAMERA_INTERFACE (raw XRGB8888 frames), named
"libretro" and given to the three cameras when the frontend offers one (outer
right and outer left "outer", inner "inner"); otherwise nothing changes.

A game's frame is the frontend's latest picture filled to the resolution it
asks, centred, flipped as it asks, in RGB565 or YUV422 (the YUV conversion of
citra_qt's camera_util.cpp, its tables copied unchanged). Black until the
first frame. Starting a camera tells the frontend which one through a private
environment command (RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_PRIVATE + 0x3D5, an "inner" or "outer"
string), so a frontend with several lenses can turn to the right one; a
frontend that does not know the command keeps its one camera for all three.

